## Why This Is Asked

This question tests ownership, bias-for-action, and customer obsession when a release harms a subset of users. It requires concrete data collection, cross-functional negotiation, and decision-making under time pressure, plus clear communication.

## Key Concepts

- Ownership and accountability under time pressure
- Data-driven impact assessment and metric selection
- Bias for action vs risk management in release engineering
- Customer-centric communication and remediation strategies

## Code Example

